A||||6||KevinP||Leaky Gas Tank||||9||
Z||000000||KevinP||09-09-2000||04:07 PM||||My gas tank has been an occasional leaker, and I have patched it once or twice before.  I finally got a real nice leak on it, and I'm leaking about a quarter tank overnight.  My question is: Is there anyplace that sells new gas tanks, or will I have to take my chances at the junkyard?  Any info appreciated.<BR>Thanks,<P>Kevin||||reg||9
Z||000001||mrfiero||09-09-2000||06:38 PM||||I doubt that you will find a brand new gas tank.  Even if you did I bet the price is outrageous.  <P>It's probably leaking from one of the tubes that runs inside (whare the gas enters the tank).  When buying a used one inspect these tubes....they should not move at all.  If they do, then the tank is no good.  <P>Obviously check everywhere else for rust and whatnot.  Good luck.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||KevinP||09-09-2000||07:39 PM||||Thanks mrfiero.  I appreciate the help.||||reg||7
Z||000003||Philphine||09-09-2000||10:02 PM||||i've had tanks off twice. the last time just last week. if you can get enough gas out and get the car as high as possible, it's not too hard. got a nice tank from kick hill for $50, plus shipping.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 09-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||09-09-2000||11:44 PM||||If you have to replace the tank.... <P>I think it's JC whitless (whitney) that has a tank treatment you might want to check out. It's suposed to stop rust and give the whole inside of the tank a coating of plastic.<P>I haven't tried the stuff yet myself. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Greg Piet||09-10-2000||01:36 AM||||Well its too bad you are not in vegas or I would GIVE you one  (minus the fuel pump)<BR>Anyone in vegas want it????||||reg||1
Z||000006||EdsB52||09-10-2000||01:59 AM||||In addition to the tubes, I would check the seam at the back of the tank. I've had 2 tanks leak there. The best fix is to replace the tank.||||reg||1
